# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: End-step phase-out and automatic untap return preserve a permanent.
# Forcing: Cast Kaito this turn so his end-step trigger is required to fire.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or battlefield and only draws lands.
# Failure modes:
#   Missing phase-out = end-step trigger or state projection failed.
#   Missing return or activation = untap return or retained loyalty failed.
#   TIMEOUT = priority or resolution failed to advance.
# Card roles:
#   Kaito Shizuki supplies the phasing trigger and a post-return activation.
#   Three lands pay his printed cost. A fourth Island and Opt hold priority.
#   Library lands prevent decking.
# Protocol path: Cast, trigger resolution, PhasedOut, PhasedIn, Activate.
[metadata]
Name:Kaito Phasing Cycle
Goal:Survive
Turns:4
Difficulty:Tutorial
Description:Cast Kaito, pass through his phase-out and return, then create a Ninja.

